Q1. What is Encapsulation? Why do we need it?

Interview Ready Answer

Encapsulation is the process of wrapping data (fields) and the methods
that operate on that data into a single unit (class) while restricting
direct access to the data using access modifiers.

Why do we need it?

• To achieve data hiding.
• To provide controlled access to data.
• To protect sensitive information.
• To perform validation before modifying data.
• To improve security.
• To improve maintainability.
• To make code more modular.

Example

class BankAccount{

    private double balance;

    public void deposit(double amount){

        if(amount > 0)
            balance += amount;
    }

    public void withdraw(double amount){

        if(amount > 0 && amount <= balance)
            balance -= amount;
    }
}

Here, balance cannot be modified directly.
The object controls all operations through methods.

