Q2. What is the difference between Encapsulation and Data Hiding?

Interview Ready Answer

Encapsulation

• Wraps data and methods into a single class.
• Controls how data is accessed.
• One of the four pillars of OOP.
• Achieved using classes and access modifiers.

Data Hiding

• Restricts direct access to data.
• Achieved mainly using access modifiers.
• Focuses only on protecting data.
• It is one of the benefits of Encapsulation.

Example

ATM Machine

Encapsulation

• ATM combines balance checking, withdrawal,
  deposit and PIN verification into one system.

Data Hiding

• User cannot directly modify account balance.
• Balance can only be changed through
  deposit() or withdraw() methods.

