INTERVIEW TRAP QUESTIONS
======================================================================

Trap 1

Question

Is Encapsulation simply making variables private
and generating getters and setters?

Correct Answer

No.

Encapsulation is the process of wrapping data and
methods into one class while controlling access to
the data.

Getters and setters are only one possible way to
provide controlled access.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

Trap 2

Question

Are getters and setters mandatory for Encapsulation?

Correct Answer

No.

They are optional.

Sometimes only business methods like

• deposit()
• withdraw()
• transfer()

are provided.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

Trap 3

Question

Is Data Hiding and Encapsulation the same?

Correct Answer

No.

Encapsulation is the mechanism.

Data Hiding is one of the benefits achieved through
Encapsulation.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

Trap 4

Question

Can a private variable be modified without a setter?

Correct Answer

Yes.

The class itself can modify its private variables
through its own methods.

Example

deposit()

withdraw()

---------------------------------------------------------------------

Trap 5

Question

Which access modifier is most commonly used to
achieve Encapsulation?

Correct Answer

private

Private fields prevent direct access from outside
the class.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

Trap 6

Question

Does Encapsulation mean data can never be accessed?

Correct Answer

No.

Encapsulation provides controlled access, not
complete inaccessibility.

Authorized methods can read or modify the data.

